{
  "abstract": "Can a Transformer train without a backward pass—zero pullbacks, VJP helpers, or same-step relays inside `with torch.no_grad():`—while beating matched-subset node perturbation? We study 3-stage delayed Weight Maximization (WM) across 162 delayed backward-free arms (`exp26`–`exp61`, plus 3 compositional, 7 pullback, and 36 BP/surrogate arms; $208$ arms $=623$ runs) on ClimbMix `d6` ($L=6,D\\in\\{256..768\\}$, $360$–$1,004$st) and Native `50.3M` ($L=8,D=512,T=2,048$, $100$st). We prove stream-partitioned WM and its $\\operatorname{diag}(1-x_i^2/D)$ `RMSNorm` mean (Prop. 1), commute $W_v$ with attention ($+0.1104\\to+0.9069$ cos, Prop. 2), route `wte` via a diagonal skip (Prop. 3), bound `RMSNorm` residual by $\\kappa_4(x)/D$ (Prop. 4), prove the 4th-moment variance drop of tangent projection (Prop. 5), and derive the Wiener-MMSE key filter $W_{\\tau,s}^{\\text{MMSE}}(M)=M A_{\\tau,s}^2/((M-1)A_{\\tau,s}^2+\\|A_{\\tau,:}\\|_2^2)$ ($3.22\\times$ key cos, Prop. 6). Fused Triton cuts `d6` WM time $38.4\\times$ ($134.31\\to3.50$ ms) and step time $8.33\\times$ ($155.6\\to18.68$ ms). Across $D\\in\\{256..768\\}$ ($360$st), 6-mat $M=4$ (`2.0794, 2.0552, 2.0451, 2.0437`; **`2.0519\\pm0.0009` Wiener-MMSE+$H_4$ at $D=384$**) attains **numerical proximity to 4-mat BP (`2.0789..2.0433`, $-0.0013$ to $+0.0020$ BPB; not 6-mat BP `2.0590..2.0153`)**. At $720$st ($D=384$), 6-mat WM hits $1.9756$ ($M=2$), $1.9672$ ($M=4, \\gamma_K=0.85$), and **$1.9632\\pm0.0006$ (`1.9284` `VAL-B`, $68.8\\%$ of 4-to-6-mat BP gain; $1.9633$ in `24.36s` via sparse Top-$K=32$) with Wiener-MMSE $M=4$**, while $840$st Upper-Half $M=2$ hits $1.9609\\pm0.0006$. On `50.3M`, Triton speeds up `fwd+rule` $6.33\\times$, hitting $1.8978$ (4-mat), $1.8853$ (6-mat $M=2$), and **$1.8849\\pm0.0003$ ($M=2$) / $1.8803\\pm0.0007$ (`1.8668` `VAL-B`, `198.42` PPL, $M=4$) on Upper-Half `(4..7)` Wiener-MMSE+$H_4$**. Short-horizon results trail 6-mat BP ($1.8904$/$1.8625$ on `d6`; $1.6989$ on `50.3M`).",
  "author": "cartan_geodesic",
  "change_summary": "1. Executed 20 new 3-seed arms (60 runs across Seeds 46, 47, 48 in exp59, exp60, exp61; total 208 multi-seed arms = 623 runs) and proved Proposition 6 (Closed-Form Parameter-Free Wiener-MMSE Key-Gather Filter, Walsh-Hadamard H_4 Temporal Multiplexing, and Sparse Top-K=32 Key Gather): Minimizing per-pair cross-key interference MSE gives W_{tau,s}^{MMSE}(M) = M A_{tau,s}^2 / ((M-1)A_{tau,s}^2 + ||A_{tau,:}||_2^2), lifting d6 6-block key cosine (M=4) 2.98x at Step 0 (0.0317 -> 0.0945) and 3.22x at Step 120 (0.0284 -> 0.0914, +25.7% over Rake; Upper-Half 3..5: 3.38x), while sparse Top-K=32 retains 99.77% of ||W^{MMSE}||_F^2 and H_4 eliminates 76.2% (48/63) of intra-head cross-coordinate interference pairs. On ClimbMix d6 (eta_K=0.024, M=4), Full 6-Mat Wiener-MMSE reaches 2.0521 +- 0.0009 DEV BPB (2.0519 +- 0.0009 with H_4, 12.20s) at 360st (66.2% of 4-to-6-mat BP gain, -0.0013 below 4-mat BP 2.0532) and 1.9632 +- 0.0006 DEV BPB (1.9284 VAL-B, 219.39 PPL, 29.14s; 1.9633 +- 0.0009 in 24.36s with sparse Top-K=32, 16.4% faster; 1.9632 +- 0.0009 in 24.54s with H_4 + Stage-2 RMSNorm leverage inversion) at 720st (68.8% of 4-to-6-mat BP gain). On Long-Context Native 50.3M (T=2,048, exp61), Upper-Half (4,5,6,7) Wiener-MMSE reaches 1.8849 +- 0.0003 DEV BPB (1.8717 VAL-B, 200.99 PPL, 5.56s/step, 9.96 GiB VRAM) at M=2—beating Full 8-Block M=2 gamma_K=0.85 (1.8853) at half the SDPA probes—and 1.8803 +- 0.0007 DEV BPB (1.8668 +- 0.0008 VAL-B, 198.42 PPL, 6.29s/step, 10.06 GiB VRAM) at M=4 with H_4, widening the gain over 4-mat exp43 (1.8978) by 1.40x (-0.0175 BPB). 2. Incorporated all 4 v9 editorial refinements: (a) 'numerical proximity to 4-mat BP' phrasing with 6-mat BP prominent; (b) pure-Python twin optimizer test + source check in verify_paper5.py; (c) ||h_n||_2 factor and exact Stage-2 leverage inversion (cos=1.000000) in Prop. 1(c); (d) trajectory archive in paper5_supplement.zip (1,986,639B) with versioned pointers to v8/v9.",
